  "fullDescription": "<p>You have a graph of <code>n</code> nodes labeled from <code>0</code> to <code>n - 1</code>. You are given an integer n and a list of <code>edges</code> where <code>edges[i] = [a<sub>i</sub>, b<sub>i</sub>]</code> indicates that there is an undirected edge between nodes <code>a<sub>i</sub></code> and <code>b<sub>i</sub></code> in the graph.</p>\n    <p>Return <code>true</code> if the edges of the given graph make up a valid tree, and <code>false</code> otherwise.</p>\n    <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n    <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 5, edges = [[0,1],[0,2],[0,3],[1,4]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> true</pre>\n    <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n    <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 5, edges = [[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[1,3],[1,4]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> false</pre>"
